{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213420,"nonce":"5llBDJGqWATef2fuQm24mIRBMvw=","title":"Feature-gate LLVM in ash so the development build does not link it","message":"inkwell is an unconditional dependency of ash_core, ash_interp and the CLI.\nThere is no feature to build without it, so every debug binary is ~200 MB and\nevery link carries LLVM 21, even for --mode interp. Incremental rebuilds after\ntouching ash_core measure about 15 s, mostly link.\n\nAdd an llvm feature, off by default for development, and make the tier and\nthe AOT path compile out cleanly without it. Zyntax's compiler crate already\nhas this shape (llvm-backend optional, Cranelift default).\n\nHot reload currently forces --jit-tier=llvm because the Cranelift tier pins a\nbytecode snapshot; until call cells make the Cranelift tier reloadable, reload\nneeds the feature on. Say so in the flag's help text.","files":null}]}